meta {
  name: List FAQs
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/faqs
  body: none
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{admin_username}}
  password: {{admin_password}}
}

docs {
  Read-only via REST (GetCollection + Get only, PUBLIC_ACCESS -- same
  conditions as AiAgent): creating/editing/deleting a FAQ only happens
  through the admin backoffice (/admin/faqs, session + CSRF), not this API.

  FaqActiveCollectionExtension filters this collection to isActive = true
  only -- draft/retired FAQs never appear here, though they still show up
  in the /admin/faqs grid (a separate Sylius query).

  Not wired into the chat/RAG pipeline: no reference to Faq in src/Chat/,
  src/KnowledgeBase/ or src/VectorConnector/ -- an agent never sees these
  entries when answering. Consumed by the frontend as suggested
  conversation-starter questions instead (frontend/composables/useFaqs.ts,
  shown on the landing page and the chat panel's empty state) -- that
  consumer further narrows the (already isActive-only) collection to FAQs
  with `highlighted: true` (JSON-LD name of Faq::$isHighlighted, editorial
  curation separate from isActive/priority).
}
